   "line": 5,
   "message": "The new rule \"a signed-out / is the marketing page, so start sign-in from /signin\" has been pasted into about 20 separate signIn helpers. These are admin, ai, ai-usage, audit, backups, backups-visual, chat, delivery, notifications, pins, retention, retention-visual, sections, suggestions and workflows, plus ask.ts. The module e2e helpers were not updated: leave, learning, payroll, time, keyflow, presales, onboarding, finance and compliance still call page.goto(to). Right now no module test signs in to \"/\", so nothing breaks. But the copies can already drift apart. Fix: have the specs import the helper from ask.ts, or another shared helper, so the rule exists in one place.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
